      "worked_solution": "The mode of a random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ is the value of $x$ at the global maxima of $f(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we can tell that $f(x)$ has a single global maximum at $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the mode of $X$ is $0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158570/assets/ec6675a5ad54923d1e0ce1b2159759d8b8be70cb4b20e82c1694c58ab49d0fb5.png)",
